# Magebane Lizard: "Whenever a player casts a noncreature spell, this creature deals damage to that player equal to the number of
# noncreature spells they've cast this turn." Turn 1: Bot1 casts Mox Ruby and Mox Emerald before the Lizard exists (no trigger
# then), casts the Lizard (a creature spell, and not on the battlefield anyway), then Mox Jet: the Lizard's controller is a player
# too, and the two Moxen cast before it entered count (the official ruling), so the damage is 3 (20 -> 17). Turn 3: the count is
# per turn: a creature spell (Llanowar Elves) draws nothing and does not count as one, and Mox Pearl is the first noncreature
# spell of the turn, 1 damage (17 -> 16).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Magebane Lizard
Llanowar Elves
Mox Pearl
Mountain
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x24

